<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Debug-only overlay. Gradle merges this into debug builds and never into
    release, which is the whole point of it living in src/debug.

    Android has blocked cleartext HTTP by default since API 28, and a debug
    APK under test talks to the dev API server over the LAN by IP — there is
    no certificate to be had for 192.168.x.x, so that traffic is plain http
    and would otherwise fail with a bare "Cleartext HTTP traffic not
    permitted" in logcat and a dead SOS screen on the phone.

    Deliberately not scoped to a single address: the laptop's DHCP lease
    changes, and a config pinned to yesterday's IP fails in a way that looks
    identical to the server being down. Release builds reach the deployed
    functions over https and are unaffected by any of this.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <application android:usesCleartextTraffic="true" />
</manifest>
